wherein (xcn-i, ycn-ι), (xcn, ycn), and (xcn+ι, ycn+ι) are the coordinates of said estimated position of said tool within the borehole at three successive said measurement times tn-ι, tn, and tn+ι, respectively; measuring acceleration signals al, a2, a3, and a4 produced by four accelerometers acl, ac2, ac3, and ac4, respectively, mounted at the ends of a first diameter of said tool and a second diameter of said tool, with said first diameter being orthogonal to said second diameter, such that accelerometers acl and ac2 are on said first diameter and accelerometers ac3 and ac4 are on said second diameter, according to the equations al = ac + a cos β + g sin α cos γ a2 = ac - a cos β - g sin α cos γ a3 = ac + a sin β - g sin α sin γ a4 = ac - a sin β + g sin α sin γ wherein ac is the centripetal acceleration of said tool, a is the lateral translational acceleration of said tool, β is the angle between said first diameter and the direction of said lateral translational acceleration, g is the earth's gravitational constant, α is the inclination angle of said tool with respect to the vertical, and γ is the angle between said first diameter and the direction of the in-plane component of gravity, g sin α;
filtering said electrical signals al, a2, a3, and a4 with a high- pass filter to produce filtered signals fal, fa2, fa3, and fa4, respectively, according to the equations fal = ac + a cos β fa2 = ac - a cos β fa3 = ac + a sin β fa4 = ac - a sin β combining said filtered signals fal, fa2, fa3, and fa4 to obtain the magnitude and direction of said lateral translational acceleration of said tool in a rotating reference frame of said tool according to the equations a = {[(fal - fa2) / (2)]2 + [(fa3 - fa4) / (2)]2}'- tan β = (fa3 - fa4) / (fal - fa2) transforming said lateral translational acceleration from said rotating reference frame of said tool into a fixed reference frame of the earth to obtain a measured lateral translational acceleration of said tool at each of said measurement times; calculating the magnitude of the difference between said derived lateral translational acceleration and said measured lateral translational acceleration according to the equation
